WEBVTT

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.510
Burnt Field (Part 1)

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.820
Um...

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.160
Uh....

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.040
I mean, what in the...

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.040
KISHOU CHAMPIONSHIP
Various Receptions Planned

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.460
The Babbling Stream Inn
Seiryuuen

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.540
It's even worse than the previous one.
I mean...

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.540
Ladies' plan includes
spa services and lunch course

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.420
The pair of Eastern shogi princes present
demonstration board commentary

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.290
Why do we have a close-up?

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.550
"The pair of eastern shogi princes"?

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.260
KISHOU CHAMPIONSHIP

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.260
I don't know about
those oval frames around you two.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:22.390
It's like photos of students who were absent
on the day of the graduation album class photo.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.390
Well, they kept taking photo after photo.

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:32.400
But then it had this "We're always
watching you from Heaven" vibe.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.410
So you tried it, then.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:44.290
It's difficult raising funds
for the Kishou Championship.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.420
I asked Nakamura, the general manager of
the Shogi Association, to come up with a design.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.170
but without spending any money,
it's a tall order.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.300
Yeah, I thought it'd be easy.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.050
Designing is tough after all.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:03.600
That's strange. I was in
the PC Club when I was in college.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:09.100
His initial enthusiasm had been so dampened
that the chairman lost it.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.190
SHOGI HALL

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.860
That's enough! It's fine!

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:17.070
STRICT BUDGET

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:17.070
NEW IDEAS

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.070
In fact, why don't we showcase
their feebleness?

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.990
We can have a stationary camera

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.490
Time Remaining
Heart Rate

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:23.620
that displays their EKG and heart rate
along with the time remaining in the match!

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:36.000
And we can have a nurse
standing by in the next room!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:40.260
Like, "If either one of them collapses,
there's nothing to worry about!"

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:43.140
Toku! Enough already!

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.640
That kind of mockery is too cruel!

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.640
PROPOSALS

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.770
This might be a relatively small-scale event,
but it's one of seven prestigious major titles!

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.770
GAP

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.110
The Kishou Championship is my life!

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:59.610
We have support from five papers, but they're all
small local newspapers so the budget was cut.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:59.610
SPONSORS
STRICT BUDGET

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:59.610
ANNOUNCEMENTS
NEW IDEAS

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.360
This is a tight period!
Surely you understand that!

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.360
GAP

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.030
69th Meijin Championship

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.740
Even at the best of times, it overlaps with
the Meijin Championship, so business is slow!

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.740
Surpass the Legend—

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.250
If we lose even more spectators and attention,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.580
from next year, the Kishou Championship...

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:14.630
GLARE

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:17.960
...will have all of its matches right here!

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.710
SHOGI HALL

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:18.710
A five-minute walk from Tokyo JR Sendagaya Station

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.100
So I appreciate your help.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.560
Whether or not next year's
Kishou Championship will be held entirely

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.860
at the Shogi Hall depends on you guys.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:40.110
So don't hold anything back.
Give a lively commentary.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.610
HAHAHAHA

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.120
These two are providing the demo board commentary.

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.610
GULP

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.120
HEAVY RESPONSIBILITY

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.120
VARIOUS
RECEPTION
PLANNER

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:52.120
But it really helped that you came.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.370
Really.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:57.130
Of course I'll do my best
with the demo board commentary!

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.210
But what's with all the gratitude, Brother?

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.050
You'll find out soon.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.560
Hey!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.560
Kan! Long time no see!

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.560
How've you been?

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.570
Kaku! Yasu! It's been a long time!

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:21.940
How are you doing?

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.780
Hey, Saku!

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.700
Kishou Yanagihara! Long time no see.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:28.700
TO THE BRIM

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:32.120
Well, here's our third pre-toast!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.710
Ready?!

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.460
Cheers!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.460
BAM

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.960
I'm thrilled to see all of you again this year.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.470
Thank you, everyone!

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:48.220
ROWDY ROWDY

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.180
Hey, Saku!

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.270
Wh-What is this?

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.610
A devious person.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:04.110
This formidable home game feeling
at the Kishou Championship.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:09.370
Most of the reporters and staffers here
are like Mr. Yanagihara's pals.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:17.370
The Kishou Championship challenger is stuck
with this awful away game feeling.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:18.670
HUG

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.880
I missed you, Saku!

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:26.470
Hey, don't be such an old goat.
I missed you too!

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.600
Geez, during this title championship,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.390
whether I take a bath, go to the salon
for coffee, or have a meal,

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.440
it's always this atmosphere.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.900
Of course it's the same
on the train going both ways.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:46.400
No matter where I go,
I hear a chorus of voices.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:50.660
The old man is shrewd that way.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:54.660
He makes himself the center of attention.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:00.670
He's 66 years old, and an active Class A player.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.960
He's won the title 14 times.

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:07.300
A true monster.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:11.930
Or after getting this far, maybe more
on the level of a vengeful ghost.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.470
An extra-large one.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:21.440
But in this fifth Kishou Championship match,
I've cornered him, 2-2.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:27.690
From the City of Shogi, Tendou,
Let's Get a Master!

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.190
I want it. I'll bite into anything I can.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.200
My first title!

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.320
I swear I'll take it.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:42.290
And with apologies to the old man,
I'm going to end his reunions!

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.100
By the way, where's Gan?

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.350
I don't see Gan.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.140
R-Right.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.730
Gan is here, but...

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.480
What? Is he ill?

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:29.510
S-Saku!

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.010
What are you doing here?
You got your match eve party.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:46.270
I got an unofficial notice,
telling me to take early retirement.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:51.440
So I left the newspaper at the end of May.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:56.530
Well, in a nutshell, I was laid off.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.750
I didn't want to cast a damper

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:08.920
on the festivities the night before your important
title match with my story of economic woe.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.300
Sorry, Saku.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.510
But Saku...

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.930
when I think about how you're still fighting,

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.020
I just couldn't sit still.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:38.070
You were lugging around
that huge camera day and night for years.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:42.080
You've done your best and then some.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:49.710
Gan, shouldn't you relax
and enjoy the rest of your life?

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:57.640
That's what my wife said. My daughter, too.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:02.680
But I'm scared.

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:07.100
Without my work, what's left for me?

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.570
I'm scared, Saku.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.910
I feel like...

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.080
I'm in a burnt field.

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.290
I'm telling you, we should use this diagram!

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:34.130
No, it's too confusing, Nikaidou!

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.010
It's better to put them up
side-by-side and explain!

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.010
FIRM
FIRM

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:39.260
We were told to keep it lively, remember?

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:39.260
UNYIELDING
UNYIELDING

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:43.520
Kiriyama, it'll go over better
if we explain with pictures!

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.270
23RD CHILDREN'S SHOGI TOURNAMENT

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.730
<i>This brings me back.</i>

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:49.270
I participated
in the Kids' Lion King Tournament too.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:52.820
And now we coach it.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:56.530
Hey, Saku. Where should I put up
the tsume-shogi problems?

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:59.030
If the kids get bored, hang them up front.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.170
Saku, I'm...

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:12.920
being demoted.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.670
My old man collapsed.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.550
I'm moving back to the countryside.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:26.520
I'm going to retire and focus on coaching kids.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.310
Saku, it's frustrating...

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:36.280
but I'm going to look for another path.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.530
Saku, please...

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:45.330
Keep fighting for us.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:50.330
We'll always, always be cheering you on.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:08.350
<i>These days, wherever I go,
I'm always the oldest one.</i>

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:11.600
<i>How long has it been like that?</i>

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:15.190
<i>Mr. Yanagihara is amazing.</i>

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:18.110
<i>He's a monster. The guy's 66 years old.</i>

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.860
<i>And still Class A. How can that be?</i>

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.490
<i>How long is he going to keep at it?</i>

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:31.540
<i>Somewhere along the line, the people
who have been fighting alongside me</i>

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:34.460
<i>have disappeared,
first one and then another.</i>

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:51.770
<i>All that's left now...</i>

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:55.520
<i>is this old body...</i>

00:12:56.690 --> 00:13:00.030
<i>and these innumerable sashes...</i>

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.740
<i>that have been entrusted to me.</i>

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:25.930
<i>They sure are heavy.</i>

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:30.020
Burnt Field (Part 1)

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:34.020
Burnt Field (Part 2)

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:39.570
<i>Well, Kishou Yanagihara,
you're the eldest active Class A player.</i>

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:42.860
<i>How long do you think you'll be able
to maintain your rank?</i>

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:45.280
<i>If you were demoted,
would you think about retiring?</i>

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.370
<i>Saku, please...</i>

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.540
<i>Keep going for our sake!</i>

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:01.840
<i>I couldn't make my dream come true,
but you can do it!</i>

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:10.060
<i>I know. I know.</i>

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:17.810
<i>The people who are departing...</i>

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:23.530
<i>don't feel like they're putting a curse on me.</i>

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:29.320
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.660
<i>I'm scared, Saku.</i>

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:42.590
<i>I feel like I'm standing in a burnt field.</i>

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.470
<i>But there are nights where...</i>

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:57.690
<i>it feels like I'll get tangled in the hundreds
of sashes I've been entrusted with.</i>

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:26.630
INTERNAL MEDICINE / EXTERNAL MEDICINE

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:44.070
Blood pressure medicine, stomach medicine...

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.650
Cataract medicine...

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:48.740
What else?

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:51.990
Ow...

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:57.250
Although I'm sure the effect
won't last to the climax of the match.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:00.670
All right.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.260
Guess I'd better get going.

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.930
SEIRYUUEN

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.890
So there's Kishou Yanagihara,

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:17.060
the eldest Class A player with his
seemingly-permanent title on the line

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.690
and Shimada 8th-Dan,
a hardworking player going for his first title.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:23.400
Who will win?

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:26.940
Whoever wins, it'll make for a bitter article.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:31.950
Quiet. Shimada 8th-Dan is here.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:41.580
GOOD LUCK, KAI

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:47.920
<i>I want to take it.</i>

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.630
<i>More than anything.</i>

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.810
<i>No matter what...</i>

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.060
<i>And it is now time to begin.</i>

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:08.400
Kishou Yanagihara,
please make the first move.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.110
Let's have a good game.

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:16.620
Black, Kishou Yanagihara, Pawn to 7-6.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:22.500
White, Shimada 8th-Dan, Pawn to 8-4.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.590
Pawn to 1-6 in his third move?

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.760
<i>An edge pawn?</i>

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.810
<i>What's he up to?</i>

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:42.390
<i>But...</i>

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.730
<i>I won't let him throw me.</i>

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:57.660
<i>He's staying on the edge?</i>

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.160
<i>Advancing like that?</i>

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.370
He's pushing on even more, with Pawn to 1-5?

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.250
That's so cool!

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:12.170
Awesome! I've seen this before!

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:13.010
In a manga!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:16.590
M-Manga? What manga?

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:21.010
<i>What a monster...</i>

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:25.020
<i>Are you saying you'll give up two moves
in exchange for my bishop?</i>

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:29.520
<i>You want to do a One-Loss Bishop Exchange?</i>

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.530
<i>But I refuse.</i>

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:35.780
<i>I'll gratefully accept your two pieces,</i>

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:38.280
<i>but I won't let you take control.</i>

00:19:02.010 --> 00:19:04.850
<i>Bishop to 2-2, promoted.</i>

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:14.360
<i>The Bishop Exchange Fourth File Rook
on the fifth move, a difficult strategy in itself,</i>

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:17.070
<i>marked the beginning of this battle.</i>

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:23.740
Is Kishou Yanagihara inviting him
to a bout of brute strength?

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:28.420
"The opening moves don't matter. If I make this
a hard fight, I'll have the upper hand."

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:30.330
Does it come from that confidence?

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:34.550
No. In response to Mr. Shimada's Pawn to 3-5,

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:38.720
he took almost no time
exchanging the 8-6 Pawn with the Rook,

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:42.140
so I think up to that point
he's already studied these moves.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:43.720
And plus...

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:47.770
this is the first time I've seen this formation.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.060
I've never seen anything like it.

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.860
<i>They both persevered.</i>

00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:59.240
<i>They both had years and years
of accumulated skill and experience.</i>

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:06.660
<i>Mr. Shimada stubbornly persisted in resisting...</i>

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.630
<i>Kishou Yanagihara's exploratory moves.</i>

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:15.250
DRAGON KING

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:15.250
LANCE

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:18.880
<i>The match approached its final stage.</i>

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:25.890
<i>The scales continued...</i>

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:30.140
<i>to tip back and forth, unrelentingly.</i>

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:32.900
SILVER GENERAL

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:40.400
GOLD
GENERAL

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:47.410
<i>And then evening came.</i>

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:50.790
He made a move.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.000
Gold to 5-8.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:56.090
Gold to 5-8!

00:20:57.670 --> 00:21:00.220
Oh, then Shimada 8th-Dan...

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:04.300
With that move,
he's gained a major advantage!

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.070
<i>Kishou... Kishou Yanagihara...</i>

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:21.030
<i>How long do you think
you can remain in Class A?</i>

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:24.700
<i>Would you think about retiring
if you were demoted from Class A?</i>

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:27.450
<i>What do you think
about the up-and-coming youngsters?</i>

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:31.580
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:36.580
<i>Without my work, what's left for me?</i>

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.590
<i>I'm scared, Saku.</i>

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:46.090
<i>I hear you, Gan.</i>

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:49.600
<i>I'm always thinking the same thing.</i>

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:53.180
<i>But I still don't have an answer.</i>

00:21:56.310 --> 00:22:01.610
<i>However, if you're standing in a burnt field,</i>

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:14.710
<i>I'm still...</i>

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:18.040
<i>burning.</i>

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:26.180
<i>Well, shall we go?</i>

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:33.520
<i>Winning and even losing</i>

00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:39.940
<i>aren't things that can ever be decided so easily.</i>

00:22:41.270 --> 00:22:44.940
<i>I'll become a human torch again today</i>

00:22:46.450 --> 00:22:49.780
<i>and give full rein to my suffering.</i>

